    <h2>What We Actually Build</h2>

    <p><a href="/">Sites On Call</a> builds websites for contractors across the Shoals. The website itself is free with an annual content plan, or available as a one-time standalone build. After that, if you want us to keep adding content each month — service pages, town pages, blog posts answering what your customers are typing into Google — we charge a monthly fee. Plans start at $149/month. No contracts. Cancel anytime.</p>

    <p>A real Shoals contractor site does the town-by-town work that most local sites skip: a Florence page that reads like you understand old-house work, a Muscle Shoals page that speaks to newer-construction service and a faster buyer, a Sheffield page that's honest about budget and repair, and coverage of the Colbert satellites — Cherokee, Leighton, Littleville — plus the Lauderdale edge communities like Killen, Rogersville, and Anderson. The threshold to compete for the real trade-plus-town searches is around 10 to 12 pages of substantive content.</p>

    <h2>Why Per-Town Pages Win the Shoals</h2>

    <p>Search "plumber Muscle Shoals AL" or "electrician Sheffield AL" and the pattern is the same across trades: a few long-tenured local contractors ranking mostly on the age of simple websites, plus the occasional Florence or out-of-town company ranking by accident because they mentioned the town once on a service-area page. Almost nobody has built a real, town-specific page targeting each customer base. That's the opening. A contractor who writes genuinely different pages for Florence, Muscle Shoals, and Sheffield — different housing, different income, different work — outranks the generic regional pages in 12 to 18 months, faster in Sheffield. For the mechanics, see our piece on <a href="/articles/local-seo-for-contractors/">local SEO for contractors</a>, and on why referrals alone stop scaling, <a href="/articles/why-word-of-mouth-isnt-enough/">why word-of-mouth isn't enough</a>.</p>

